body: "## Current-head hosted evidence\nAt PR #46 head `5a853daa462d1766061edc26789c30f0fdeec46f`, the full [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40583097964/job/122467426453) reports 722 tests, 714 passing and eight failing. [Node 26](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40583097964/job/122467426662) independently reports the same terminal-import and seeded assignee-preservation assertion classes. The npm and Bun release jobs are also failed. These are hosted synthetic test results, not a live Azure incident or a local crash reproduction.\n\nSeveral existing terminal-import/close recovery tests now return `ADO_CONFLICT` with “Native item history advanced; re-read both trackers and retry” where successful terminal reconciliation is expected:\n- terminal states import (test/sync.test.ts:686);\n- import-close boundary matrix (:1477);\n- native close assignment recovery (:2596);\n- unassigned terminal close recovery (:2699);\n- canonical status aliases after close interruption (:3004).\n\nThe unchanged 512-sequence model also fails at seed `3404983668`, sequence `326`: “lost assignee edit”. The retained diagnostic shows an empty remote-assignee edit pending, a failed `ADO_REMOTE` attempt, then a resumed success exporting assignee and iteration-path. This establishes a failed preservation oracle, not yet its root cause or evidence of customer data loss. Coverage failures remain additional gate failures, not the explanation for these eight functional failures.\n\n## Source goal and scope\nThe [canonical SDK adoption item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/blob/5a853daa462d1766061edc26789c30f0fdeec46f/.agents/pm/chores/pm-ado-sdk-adoption.toon) requires native lifecycle preservation, preserved concurrent edits and unchanged full acceptance gates. The [accepted R8 fallback](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/blob/5a853daa462d1766061edc26789c30f0fdeec46f/.agents/pm/issues/pm-ado-sdk-history-fence.toon) explicitly permits post-write verification/append-only compensation pending upstream pm-cli#1576. This report does not reject that accepted design or label compensation equivalent to pre-write CAS.\n\nThe changed [history-fence.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/blob/5a853daa462d1766061edc26789c30f0fdeec46f/history-fence.ts) verifies an exact native head and propagates `NativeHistoryConflict`; [sync.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/blob/5a853daa462d1766061edc26789c30f0fdeec46f/sync.ts#L433-L446) routes scalar, prepared close, terminal transition and assignment through the fenced writer. These are investigation locations, not a proven causal diagnosis.\n\n## Expected / impact\nSupported terminal reconciliation should preserve native close semantics and mapped assignment/recovery without refusing its own legitimate native history. The seeded two-sided model must preserve every pending user edit through failure and resume. Current full gates fail these assertions despite focused history-fence checks passing, so PR #46 is not release-certified.\n\n## Acceptance / regression\n- Minimize the terminal-conflict cases and seed 3404983668 / sequence 326 using the existing synthetic fixtures; identify whether implementation or an evidenced invalid oracle is responsible.\n- Keep the monotonic native-history fence, fail-closed stale/ABA refusal, complete native lifecycle effects and append-only audit history. Do not weaken the guard merely to make these tests pass.\n- Preserve an empty assignee edit as a real edit through failure/retry; retain terminal native assignment clearing and mapped recovery distinctions.\n- Rerun the existing failing tests, the complete model, native-precondition/verification checks and full Node 22/26 npm/Bun gates on one immutable head, retaining coverage thresholds.\n- Report provider, crash and artifact verification separately. No live Azure writes were performed for this review.\n\nDeduplication: all 59 all-status GitHub issue/PR records, PR conversation/inline/review records and the current SDK adoption/history-fence/terminal-match PM items were checked. #59 is the prior coverage-only failure on an older revision; pm-cli#1576 is the missing upstream pre-write API. Neither is this current full-suite functional failure outcome. PR #46 and pm-ado-sdk-adoption remain the implementation owners.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-27T22:17:16Z)\n>\n> ## Functional failures superseded on the latest PR head; coverage remains incomplete\n> \n> At PR #46 head `5ea8a8257d69104f69545b49eab71f762ab8889e`, both current hosted jobs report **770 tests, 770 passing, zero failing**:\n> - [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40589672134/job/122490306154)\n> - [Node 26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40589672134/job/122490306129)\n> \n> The prior eight functional failures at `5a853daa` are therefore superseded by current-head evidence. The jobs still fail at **99.79% branch coverage against the unchanged 100% threshold**, so this is not a clean full release gate or a publication claim.\n> \n> The source delta adds a locked SDK audit witness for successful equivalent native updates, classifies SDK exceptions against the captured immutable history head, and removes forced lease takeover from verification. The new hosted cases explicitly cover equivalent updates, peer audits, errors after a real write, and waiting for a live peer lease. The seeded preservation sequence and terminal-import cases now pass.\n> \n> Independent bounded check: Node 24.22.1, exact `NativeWriteFence` class with a deterministic in-memory SDK mock, **24 assertions across five schedules**: successful no-op, peer-before-no-op, stable SDK error, peer-advanced SDK error, and an ordinary own event. This confirms the local branching/receipt behavior, not real SDK transaction durability, provider concurrency, live lease behavior or crash recovery.\n> \n> Keep the existing acceptance criteria and fail-closed history guards. Remaining work is the coverage gate and any broader acceptance evidence required by the implementation owner; no customer-data-loss or released-regression claim is made.\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-28T00:37:37Z)\n>\n> ## Latest exact-head gates now pass\n> \n> PR #46 remains at `23c2b2bbed53eeeaffe201b72e816de87d758a4f`. Its current Node 22, Node 26, npm and Bun release gates are successful. The [npm gate log](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40601295245/job/122529790619) records 776/776 V8 tests and 776/776 AST tests, zero failures, 100% line/branch/function coverage, 2328/2328 statements across 13 source files, followed by 19/19 native acceptance tests.\n> \n> This supersedes the earlier 99.79% branch-coverage blocker as well as the original eight functional failures. The previously recorded 31-assertion in-memory SDK journal/payload probe is reused at this unchanged source revision, not rerun.\n> \n> Limits: this is verified hosted evidence for the exact PR head, not npm publication, merge approval, or independent real-provider/concurrency/crash certification. Preserve the accepted fail-closed history guards and existing acceptance criteria. No new defect or customer-data-loss claim is made."
